# ESP32-2432S028 "Cheap Yellow Display": classic ESP32-WROOM-32 with 4 MB flash.
# 320x240 ST7789 on SPI2, backlight on GPIO 21, BOOT as the only button.
# No PSRAM, no microphone, speaker, touch or PMIC. Pins: docs/hardware.md#esp32-2432s028-cyd-cheap-yellow-display
CONFIG_IDF_TARGET="esp32"
# The base file selects 4 MB; this board uses the same 4 MB flash (no override needed).
# There is no PSRAM and the full 320x240 framebuffer (150 KB) does not fit, so
# the port reserves a 320x120 band (75 KB) in an early constructor and the UI
# renders the screen in bands of that size (port_display.cpp, Display::framebuffer_rows).
# CONFIG_SPIRAM is not set
CONFIG_HG_BOARD_ESP32_CYD=y
